1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:02,836
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:14,305
<i>Hello, Raul. Come back here.</i>
<i>I have a surprise for you.</i>

3
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:16,641
[Raul] <i>What are you talking about, Emilia?</i>

4
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,435
[tires screeching]

5
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:20,603
[crying] <i>Jasmin!</i>

6
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,564
-<i>I'm here!</i>
-[Emilia laughing]

7
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:26,568
<i>Diego! Diego, help us, please!</i>
<i>My mother needs help!</i>

8
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,527
<i>Please! Please!</i>

9
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,612
-<i>I'll kill you!</i>
-[Jepoy] <i>I'm her bodyguard.</i>

10
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:30,739
<i>I won't let you hurt her.</i>

11
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,866
[Ivy] <i>To San Joaquin.</i>
<i>My mom will be safe there.</i>

12
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:37,370
[Julio] <i>You'll be running</i>
<i>for senator in my place.</i>

13
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>You need Ivy's money</i>
<i>for our plans to push through.</i>

14
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:42,876
[Diego] <i>Are you Lily?</i>

15
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,378
<i>Are Ivy Aguas and Lily Cruz</i>
<i>the same person?</i>

16
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,756
<i>Yes, Diego. I'm your old friend.</i>

17
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:50,967
-[Diego] <i>Why did you lie to me?</i>
-<i>I have my reasons.</i>

18
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:54,763
<i>And even if I told you,</i>
<i>you wouldn't understand.</i>

19
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,766
[Jepoy] <i>There were no charred</i>
<i>remains in the building.</i>

20
00:00:57,849 --> 00:00:59,225
<i>-Not one.</i>
<i>-That's impossible!</i>

21
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:02,353
<i>Don't stop until you can</i>
<i>show me a dead body.</i>

22
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:05,857
[Ivy] <i>Every time I see her suffering,</i>

23
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:09,861
<i>I remember the people who made her suffer.</i>

24
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:12,447
<i>Ivy, whatever your plans are,</i>
<i>I'll help you.</i>

25
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,573
<i>Because I love you.</i>

26
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:15,492
[Ivy] <i>You don't know what</i>
<i>you're saying, Diego.</i>

27
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,868
-[Diego] <i>Mrs. Camia…</i>
-[Camia] <i>Raul, you bastard!</i>

28
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:19,245
<i>If it weren't for you,</i>
<i>I wouldn't be like this!</i>

29
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,246
<i>Get away from me!</i>

30
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,873
[Diego] <i>Ivy, is it true</i>
<i>my dad's the reason</i>

31
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,875
<i>your mother's this way now?</i>

32
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:28,004
<i>Yes! My mother is like that</i>
<i>because of Raul!</i>

33
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:30,131
<i>Because of your good-for-nothing father!</i>

34
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:35,845
[tense music playing]

35
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:45,271
[tires screeching]

36
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:46,564
[gasps]

37
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:50,068
Don't step out of the car
no matter what happens, okay?

38
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:55,990
Good grief. Why can't we leave the house

39
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,409
without being bothered by the Ardientes?

40
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:05,375
Stay alert.

41
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:19,848
[uneasily] Uh… What's this about, Mayor?

42
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,350
[Arnaldo] I talked to Miss Aguas
on the phone,

43
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:24,227
and I know she's on vacation.

44
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,104
I need to know exactly where she is.

45
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,606
With all due respect, Mayor,

46
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,860
she wants to have some time alone.

47
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:35,363
That's the thing. She's alone.
And Ivy is a woman.

48
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,365
She needs someone to protect her.

49
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:41,870
Oh, Ivy doesn't need a man to protect her.

50
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:46,040
She can defend herself.
Besides, she's with…

51
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:49,961
With whom, Carlotta?

52
00:02:51,754 --> 00:02:55,925
Tell me, who is with Miss Aguas?

53
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,428
[suspenseful music playing]

54
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:03,349
[Ivy] That's the truth!

55
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:07,103
For 13 years, he kept my mother hidden.

56
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:09,772
Ivy, wait. I don't understand.

57
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,108
Why would my dad do that to your mother?

58
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:14,611
You want answers
but can't connect the dots?

59
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,779
Well, I don't understand either, Diego!

60
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:20,867
When we were kids,
your father tried to rape my mother.

61
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:23,703
Did you forget about that, Diego?!

62
00:03:24,829 --> 00:03:28,583
Okay, let me remind you.
I'll tell you everything!

63
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,339
My family moved to Poblacion Ardiente…

64
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:40,220
<i>because we thought our lives</i>
<i>would be better there.</i>

65
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,264
[Julio] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

66
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:46,726
-[all] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>
-<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

67
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,978
[all] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

68
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,480
[Ivy] <i>Little did we know…</i>

69
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:54,943
the leaders of that town were all evil!

70
00:03:58,196 --> 00:04:03,868
Then, one day Raul tried
to rape my mother.

71
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,121
-[Lily] <i>Mom.</i>
-<i>Dad.</i>

72
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:07,956
<i>You bastard!</i>

73
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:11,376
-[Lily] <i>Dad! Dad!</i>
-[Diego] <i>Dad! Dad! Dad!</i>

74
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:13,002
-[Dante groaning]
-Dad!

75
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:15,004
-[Camia] <i>Leave us alone!</i>
-[Lily] <i>Stop it!</i>

76
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:16,589
<i>I'll file a case against you.</i>

77
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:18,466
[Ivy] <i>Yes, Diego.</i>

78
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,344
<i>That's when it all started.</i>

79
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:26,766
That's how my family met its ruin.

80
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:28,893
All because of your father.

81
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:34,357
When my father learned about it,
he tried to seek justice.

82
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:40,071
But after he spoke to Emilia,
what happened to him?

83
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:45,910
<i>He died. Or should I say…</i>

84
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,621
<i>he was killed!</i>

85
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:52,875
<i>You killed my husband!</i>
<i>You murderers! Get out of here!</i>

86
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:54,627
[Ivy] <i>Would you believe…</i>

87
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,338
he died of a heart attack?

88
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:01,259
After my father died,

89
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,386
did you know what they did to my mother?

90
00:05:03,469 --> 00:05:05,847
She was raped and tortured!

91
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,057
-[shushes]
-[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>

92
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:12,854
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

93
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:18,109
So, for 13 years, I thought
both my parents were dead!

94
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:20,445
I thought I was all alone!

95
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:23,573
So, once more…

96
00:05:24,907 --> 00:05:28,578
Your worthless father raped my mother!

97
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:34,250
And your mother had
both my parents killed!

98
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,169
Even me, Diego!
She tried to have me killed!

99
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:41,132
You heard me right, Diego.
She wanted me dead!

100
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:44,260
[young Lily crying] <i>No! Please don't!</i>

101
00:05:45,344 --> 00:05:50,391
Your grandfather, your mother,
and your father,

102
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:53,770
the people who rule Poblacion Ardiente,

103
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:59,067
they had us slaughtered
like we were animals.

104
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,028
All of them, Diego.

105
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,741
[tense music playing]

106
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:13,623
Lily, I'm sorry. I didn't know.

107
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,541
I tried to find you.

108
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,502
Believe me, Lily. I looked for you.

109
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:18,711
And if I'd found you,

110
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,713
you wouldn't have suffered alone.

111
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:24,884
You can't do anything about it,
Diego. The damage has been done.

112
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,932
Is that why you came back here?

113
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,769
To get back at my family?

114
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:41,234
Ivy, seeking revenge won't solve anything.

115
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:43,027
It'll only be harder on you.

116
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,196
Just leave.

117
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,407
-Ivy, listen to me--
-I said get out!

118
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,785
I want you to go. Get out!

119
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:54,997
I said out!

120
00:06:56,332 --> 00:06:57,458
Ivy, I'm sorry.

121
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:02,088
[dramatic music playing]

122
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:05,800
[sighs]

123
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,973
[sobbing]

124
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,667
I knew it.

125
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:44,255
Diego is with Miss Aguas.

126
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,466
Those two traitors.

127
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:50,803
I can smell them
from miles away. They stink!

128
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:52,847
Don't worry, Grandpa.

129
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,766
We'll make Diego tell us
where he's hiding Ivy.

130
00:07:56,642 --> 00:08:00,897
And I'm sure the people from the
co-op know where my brother is.

131
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:06,861
If we need to burn that place
and tear down the houses,

132
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:10,823
including those beggars
living there, then do it.

133
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:13,451
If that's what it takes for us
to know where those two are.

134
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:15,870
[Julio sighs]

135
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:18,831
[Jepoy] Mr. Fred.

136
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:32,720
[suspenseful music playing]

137
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:39,310
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy, Emilia doesn't know anything.</i>

138
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:44,398
<i>Even though we're apart and</i>
<i>Emilia's keeping an eye on me,</i>

139
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,984
<i>no Ardiente will lay a finger on you.</i>

140
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:48,986
<i>I'm still yours, Ivy.</i>

141
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:51,697
Mister Fred.

142
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,492
-I'll leave it to you.
-Okay. Thank you.

143
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:55,952
-Just do the usual.
-Okay.

144
00:09:01,999 --> 00:09:03,960
[suspenseful music playing]

145
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:10,132
[Loring] We really don't know
where Diego is.

146
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:12,385
He hasn't come home in a few days.

147
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,263
Why are you looking for him?

148
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:19,141
I'm sure that he's with Miss Aguas.

149
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:22,103
Or…

150
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:25,106
I could be wrong.

151
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:30,695
Maybe you're the one
hiding that two-faced woman.

152
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,031
-No, we're not.
-We're not hiding her.

153
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,533
[chuckles]

154
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:42,373
But aren't you on her side now
because she bought you land?

155
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:47,461
That obviously means you work for her now.

156
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:53,009
That also means you love her now.

157
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:56,262
-It's not like that.
-[Julio] No.

158
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:57,972
-It's just…
-We're not…

159
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:00,600
[shushes]

160
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,185
There's no need to explain.

161
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:06,063
I'm still your Señor Julio.

162
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:10,943
And my prodigal children
need to be punished.

163
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:17,742
If you don't tell me
where Miss Ivy Aguas is…

164
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:21,078
you'll see what I'm capable of.

165
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:25,750
Congressman, we really don't
know anything about this.

166
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,585
[Loring] We don't know.

167
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,629
-We don't know where she is!
-We don't know.

168
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,380
[Fernan] We aren't hiding her.

169
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,801
[tense music playing]

170
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:44,602
[tires screeching]

171
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,692
[screams]

172
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:57,490
[young Lily crying] <i>Why did Mom</i>
<i>say… they killed Dad?</i>

173
00:10:57,573 --> 00:11:01,702
-[young Diego] <i>I didn't know.</i>
-<i>He's dead!</i>

174
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,996
[Loring] <i>Come on. Come on. Sorry, Lily.</i>

175
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,706
[young Diego wailing]

176
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,833
[young Diego]
<i>They said a crime took place.</i>

177
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:10,961
<i>Daddy, you know a lot of cops, right?</i>

178
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:14,924
<i>-Let's find Lily.</i>
<i>-You know, Diego…</i>

179
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:15,966
<i>It's better if</i>

180
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,135
<i>you don't expect to ever see Lily again.</i>

181
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:24,392
-[Julio] <i>You idiot!</i>
-<i>What did I do, Grandpa?</i>

182
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,852
<i>You caused a huge scandal!</i>

183
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:29,772
<i>Because of you,</i>
<i>people are talking about a child</i>

184
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:33,192
<i>who's gone missing</i>
<i>from Poblacion Ardiente!</i>

185
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:37,321
[tense music playing]

186
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:46,956
[Diego] <i>My whole life, I thought</i>
<i>my family could still change.</i>

187
00:11:48,999 --> 00:11:53,129
<i>But if they don't,</i>
<i>I'll turn my back on them.</i>

188
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:57,758
<i>I'll help you get justice, Ivy.</i>

189
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:01,095
[tense music playing]

190
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,228
[Claire] Raul.

191
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:15,484
[sighs] Drunk again.
Look at this mess. Good grief.

192
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,736
Ma'am, for Mr. Raul.

193
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,405
-What's this?
-A letter.

194
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:21,240
Thank you.

195
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,164
[Emilia] Aunt Claire, what's that?

196
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:31,834
[suspenseful music playing]

197
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,171
A summons for Raul.

198
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:37,339
Someone filed a report against him.

199
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:44,889
[Dr. Faustino] Try to color
within the lines.

200
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,640
Can you do that, Camia?

201
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:51,187
[slow instrumental playing]

202
00:12:56,066 --> 00:12:56,984
Mom.

203
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,196
Ivy.

204
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:08,913
I'm glad you still remember my name.

205
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:18,088
Uh… I'll leave you here with Ivy, then.

206
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:19,590
Okay, Doc.

207
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:24,803
Ivy?

208
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,307
You look sad.

209
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,310
Where is Diego?

210
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:34,772
Did you two have a fight?

211
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:40,486
Diego had somewhere to be.

212
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,531
Where did he go?

213
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:53,958
Don't worry about that, Mom.
You have to focus on your rehab.

214
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,668
Hopefully, you'll get better soon.

215
00:13:57,586 --> 00:13:59,004
You'll get better, right?

216
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,216
Yes, Ivy.

217
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:05,553
For you, I will.

218
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,182
[slow instrumental playing]

219
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,619
-Sir, where are you going?
-I want to talk to Dad.

220
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:31,996
Mr. Raul's not here.

221
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:36,125
Dad! Dad!

222
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:41,964
Diego. Seems like you're
barking up the wrong house.

223
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,549
[chuckles]

224
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,553
I went to the co-op.

225
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:51,390
It's been a few days
since they last saw you.

226
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:53,100
Where did you go?

227
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,563
I had something to take care of, Grandpa.

228
00:14:58,564 --> 00:14:59,732
Well…

229
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:02,818
I need details.

230
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:05,446
[stutters] Co-op business.

231
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:06,822
[chuckles]

232
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:11,201
Come on, Diego. Don't lie to me.

233
00:15:13,829 --> 00:15:15,956
You were with Ivy Aguas, weren't you?

234
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,458
[suspenseful sting]

235
00:15:18,792 --> 00:15:20,044
Who told you that?

236
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:22,963
I don't even know where Ivy is.

237
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,049
Perhaps…

238
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:28,886
you'll tell me the truth if I told you…

239
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:34,099
that the lives of your friends
at the cooperative…

240
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:36,977
depend on it.

241
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:41,982
Grandpa, I'm begging you.
Leave the farmers out of this.

242
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:44,777
-I don't know where Ivy is!
-[chuckles]

243
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,823
I will ask you one last time.

244
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:54,119
Where is Ivy Aguas?

245
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:57,665
[tense music playing]

246
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,629
I don't know where she is, Grandpa.

247
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:07,466
Oh, well.

248
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:11,887
Very well, then.

249
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:15,432
[tense music playing]

250
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,192
[Diego] Nanny?

251
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:27,069
Hey.

252
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:31,824
Nanny, I know Grandpa
came here to threaten you.

253
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:34,702
I'm sorry for dragging you into this mess.

254
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:36,787
Your grandpa's insane.

255
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:41,000
He told us you know
where Miss Aguas really is.

256
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:42,835
I just find it ridiculous.

257
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:46,630
[bleak music playing]

258
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:50,259
Diego, what's wrong?

259
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,386
Is there something we should know?

260
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,764
Nanny, I'm sorry.

261
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,184
But I can't answer that question.

262
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:01,437
What kind of answer is that, Diego?

263
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:05,691
Well, then remember this.

264
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:12,614
No matter what happens, we'll
always be here for you, okay?

265
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:17,369
Nanny, thank you.

266
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,126
Aunt Claire.

267
00:17:24,209 --> 00:17:26,253
You have to help me get out of here.

268
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,338
[Claire] Where are you going?

269
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:29,757
[Emilia sighs] I need to find out

270
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,717
who filed the police report against Raul.

271
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:35,763
-[Claire] But why?
-Because I have to protect him.

272
00:17:36,805 --> 00:17:41,810
Emilia, you'd disobey your
father again just for that man?

273
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:45,105
Oh, Emilia, when will you ever learn?

274
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:51,320
[sighs] I'll take care of it.
Leave it to your Aunt Clarita.

275
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,867
[man] You're not allowed to leave, sir.

276
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:05,000
Even there? Please?
Do you know who Camia is?

277
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:09,922
Can't you understand
what I feel right now?

278
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:11,131
Or not?

279
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,550
You don't know her, right?

280
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:19,014
-That's why you guys--
-[bottle shatters]

281
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,974
That's why you guys can do this to me!

282
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,062
[panting]

283
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:30,317
[crying] You know nothing…
You know nothing at all.

284
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,611
You don't know how it hurts me.

285
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:36,240
[sobbing] Camia…

286
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:49,837
[tense music playing]

287
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,985
-[Camia] <i>There's a fire!</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Mom…</i>

288
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,778
[Camia coughs] <i>Fire!</i>

289
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,739
[Camia] <i>Fire!</i>

290
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,367
[Camia and Ivy gasping]

291
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:21,910
[Ivy coughs]

292
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:24,830
[Camia coughing]

293
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:28,834
[suspenseful music playing]

294
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:37,467
-[panting] Fire!
-Mom! Mom?

295
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:39,636
-Mom.
-Fire! Fire!

296
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,013
-Mom, there's no fire.
-Fire!

297
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:43,640
-Fire! Fire!
-Mom, there's no fire. Nurse!

298
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:45,017
-Nurse!
-Fire…

299
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,268
-Mom, there's no fire.
-Fire…

300
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:47,728
-Mom, there's no fire.
-Fire!

301
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:51,190
Mom, sit down. Mom. Mom. You're safe here.

302
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:52,524
Shh… Nurse.

303
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:55,861
-There's a fire.
-Mom.

304
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:57,946
[Camia panting]

305
00:20:01,783 --> 00:20:06,747
Shh… Mom, you're safe here.
You're safe, Mom.

306
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:09,833
[dramatic music playing]

307
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:17,674
Doc, isn't there any way
to speed up my mom's recovery?

308
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:20,802
As I see it, she's only getting worse!

309
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,888
Miss Aguas, I have to remind you

310
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:24,806
that this is not going to be easy.

311
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:29,186
I'm really sorry, but she has
far too many painful memories,

312
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:32,689
which were trapped in her mind
for 13 years.

313
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:34,358
It's very hard for her.

314
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,360
So, what do you mean?

315
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:38,946
That there's no chance
my mom will ever recover?

316
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:43,200
Doc, tell me the truth.
I need to know the truth!

317
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,119
Is this a hopeless case?

318
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:50,999
I have to be honest with you, Miss Aguas.

319
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:53,961
Only a miracle can cure her now.

320
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,838
[ominous music playing]

321
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:03,595
Madrigal, no one must ever know
what you might hear tonight.

322
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,389
Especially Julio.

323
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:07,057
Yes, ma'am.

324
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:08,892
Let him off, Auntie.

325
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:10,727
Madrigal is loyal to me.

326
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:13,522
Where is that woman?

327
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:26,618
-Belen? Belen, right?
-Yes.

328
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:31,581
I am Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

329
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:35,377
Former governor of Poblacion Ardiente.

330
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:41,925
Just to let you know,
I care for the masses.

331
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:44,136
I don't want them taken advantage of,

332
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:47,597
so even if Raul is my husband…

333
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,850
if he's done something wrong…

334
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:52,102
he must be punished.

335
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:57,691
What did Raul do?
Why did you file a complaint?

336
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:02,487
He kidnapped Jasmin and hid her.

337
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:06,199
"Jasmin"?

338
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,744
[Dr. Faustino]
But there's another treatment

339
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:09,745
that we haven't done yet.

340
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:11,288
It's called the ECT.

341
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:15,959
ECT? Electroconvulsive therapy?

342
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:19,838
You'll induce a brain seizure
in my mother?

343
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:21,965
Doc, isn't that dangerous?

344
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,092
No, it's considered safe.

345
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:27,679
But usually, it's the
last resort for cases like this.

346
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:30,140
How will that affect my mother?

347
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,977
Well, yet again I need to be
honest with you, Miss Aguas.

348
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:37,189
There are risks involved
in using this treatment.

349
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:40,317
She might suffer permanent memory loss.

350
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,986
Or her condition could become much worse.

351
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:47,407
But there is also a possibility
that she'll get better.

352
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:49,701
Are you saying that

353
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:53,371
I'd be risking my mother's
mental health on a procedure

354
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:55,165
that has no guarantee of success?

355
00:22:55,749 --> 00:22:56,708
Is that it?

356
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:00,712
[exhales]

357
00:23:04,466 --> 00:23:07,677
[Belen] Raul brought her to me
to take care of her.

358
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:10,764
That was 13 years ago.

359
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:14,142
She had a gunshot wound
and wasn't herself.

360
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:21,358
But when she started to get better,
Raul suddenly changed.

361
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:25,946
He kept Jasmin locked up.
He wouldn't let her out.

362
00:23:26,738 --> 00:23:28,365
Not even to see a doctor.

363
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:32,285
And one time,
I tried helping Jasmin escape,

364
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:35,288
but Raul hurt me too.

365
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:37,415
[tense music playing]

366
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:40,752
Do you know what Jasmin's full name is?

367
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:41,837
No, ma'am.

368
00:23:43,046 --> 00:23:45,757
But there was a woman I spoke to

369
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:48,093
who called Jasmin by another name.

370
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:51,346
She called her…

371
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:53,640
Camia.

372
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:59,062
[dramatic music playing]

373
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:04,359
[Belen] She was beautiful,
tall, and fair-skinned.

374
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:09,364
You might've seen her.
Please help me find her.

375
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:11,324
Camia?

376
00:24:12,909 --> 00:24:15,662
[tense music playing]

377
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:22,627
-[Emilia] Raul.
-[Raul] What?

378
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:29,009
Where are you hiding her?

379
00:24:29,801 --> 00:24:32,637
Did you let her escape again? Answer me!

380
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:35,515
What are you talking about?

381
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:39,895
I'm not hiding anything
or anyone! She's dead!

382
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:43,690
I could kill you right now, you liar!

383
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,735
Why do you want to kill me?
Camia's gone, she's dead!

384
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,445
Isn't that what you want to hear?

385
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:51,323
Thirteen years, Raul.

386
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:54,743
You made me believe that you changed.

387
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:58,705
Until I found out you had another secret!

388
00:24:58,788 --> 00:25:00,498
Why are you so obsessed with her?

389
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:05,295
Because I love Camia.

390
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:14,763
And the truth is, you'll never understand

391
00:25:14,846 --> 00:25:16,598
how much I love her.

392
00:25:17,807 --> 00:25:19,809
[dramatic music playing]

393
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:22,979
[sobbing]

394
00:25:32,155 --> 00:25:34,908
-Are you done?
-I loved you, Raul.

395
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:38,495
I still love you.

396
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:41,122
I gave you everything. Everything!

397
00:25:41,206 --> 00:25:43,541
Until I had nothing left for myself!

398
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,961
This is the thanks I get?

399
00:25:47,837 --> 00:25:49,464
Kill me now!

400
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:54,594
-Kill me now! Just kill me now!
-Make her stop.

401
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:00,016
[Emilia weeping]

402
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:03,520
That's enough. Let's go. Emilia.

403
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:06,690
[Emilia weeping]

404
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:24,082
[bleak music playing]

405
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,181
[tense music playing]

406
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:42,851
Mom, I spoke to your doctor.

407
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:48,690
She told me there's something
we haven't tried yet.

408
00:26:49,607 --> 00:26:50,900
A procedure.

409
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:54,487
[sighs] But then…

410
00:26:58,074 --> 00:27:01,119
There's no guarantee
the procedure will work.

411
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:06,333
I don't want to risk your mental health.

412
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:12,339
I don't want your memories to disappear.

413
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:16,843
[sighs heavily]

414
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:23,516
Ivy. Are you crying?

415
00:27:25,226 --> 00:27:26,186
Why?

416
00:27:26,936 --> 00:27:28,730
Don't be sad.

417
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:32,484
Take this so you'll feel better.

418
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:39,115
Don't be afraid, okay?

419
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:41,493
Don't be sad.

420
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:42,994
Fight.

421
00:27:43,953 --> 00:27:46,623
Hope. Change.

422
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,877
That's what I learned from my husband.

423
00:27:56,466 --> 00:27:57,467
Mom?

424
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:03,807
Mom.

425
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:14,150
[bleak music playing]

426
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:22,075
What is it, Diego? Why are you here?

427
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:26,621
Do you want to judge me too?
Go and judge me all you want!

428
00:28:26,704 --> 00:28:30,208
Say what you want to say!
Tell me all of my mistakes!

429
00:28:30,834 --> 00:28:31,835
Well?

430
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:35,547
Why did you do it?

431
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:40,635
What?

432
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,013
What did I do? What do you mean?

433
00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:45,890
Why did you do that to Mrs. Camia?

434
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:49,477
Why did you take advantage of her?

435
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:50,979
Why did you cage her like an animal?

436
00:28:51,062 --> 00:28:52,480
Why didn't you take her to a doctor?

437
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,065
I thought you loved her!

438
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:57,110
-Yes, I love Camia!
-Do you?

439
00:28:57,444 --> 00:29:00,363
What kind of love is that?
Tell me the truth.

440
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:04,117
Why did you do that?
Why did you do that, Dad?!

441
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:06,995
Diego, listen to me. Yes, I admit.

442
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:10,248
I'm the reason
why her family's all dead now.

443
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:14,919
I'm the reason
Emilia massacred her family.

444
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:17,589
But they were wrong. Camia survived!

445
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:22,761
When I found her, I saved her!
I saved her!

446
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,638
I hid her from Emilia
because I love Camia!

447
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:30,018
[sighs] Doc, I don't understand.

448
00:29:30,226 --> 00:29:32,604
I can talk to her like my mother.

449
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:34,981
Maybe there's a chance she'll get better.

450
00:29:35,064 --> 00:29:39,110
Maybe she doesn't need to undergo ECT.

451
00:29:39,194 --> 00:29:40,737
But that is not a clear indication

452
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:42,238
that she's feeling better.

453
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:46,242
Sometimes, patients with
temporary memory loss

454
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:50,371
experience having false memories,
invented memories,

455
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:52,874
real memories misplaced in time.

456
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:54,125
[exhales]

457
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:57,337
So, she still needs to undergo an ECT?

458
00:29:57,712 --> 00:29:59,130
In other cases,

459
00:29:59,214 --> 00:30:02,884
the family accepts the patient's condition

460
00:30:02,967 --> 00:30:07,055
and they just improve the
quality of life of the patient.

461
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:10,141
But in your case,
if you want to fight it out,

462
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:13,728
we've yet to try
electroconvulsive therapy.

463
00:30:15,939 --> 00:30:16,940
[sighs]

464
00:30:18,024 --> 00:30:21,528
Please consider this,
Miss Aguas. For your mother.

465
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:27,116
-Thank you. You may go now.
-Okay.

466
00:30:28,201 --> 00:30:30,203
[tense music playing]

467
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:34,958
[exhales]

468
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:39,754
We have a pressing matter, Auntie.

469
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:41,840
I need to find that Camia.

470
00:30:42,465 --> 00:30:43,466
I don't understand.

471
00:30:44,133 --> 00:30:46,886
All this trouble to find Raul's mistress?

472
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:50,014
Because I'm the one who had her killed…

473
00:30:50,723 --> 00:30:52,392
she can ruin our family's name.

474
00:30:52,475 --> 00:30:55,562
I need to bury her back
in the grave she crawled out of!

475
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:57,438
[ominous music playing]

476
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:11,995
Are they fighting again?
Or just watching a soap opera?

477
00:31:12,078 --> 00:31:13,079
[Arnaldo sighs]

478
00:31:16,165 --> 00:31:22,755
Well, I can sense that you want
to tell me what the problem is.

479
00:31:24,007 --> 00:31:26,885
Come on. Spit it out, grandson.

480
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:29,971
Camia Cruz…

481
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:34,767
a woman Mom killed a long time ago.

482
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:37,562
She's still alive.

483
00:31:37,687 --> 00:31:39,230
[suspenseful sting]

484
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:54,203
What you did was wrong.
My whole life, Dad.

485
00:31:54,704 --> 00:31:57,624
My whole life, you made me
believe you were a good man.

486
00:32:00,084 --> 00:32:02,128
But it was all you.

487
00:32:02,795 --> 00:32:04,881
If you hadn't gone after Mrs. Camia,

488
00:32:04,964 --> 00:32:07,008
this wouldn't have happened to Lily.

489
00:32:07,091 --> 00:32:08,718
She was my best friend.

490
00:32:08,801 --> 00:32:11,554
You did this to my best friend!
How could you do this?!

491
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:13,181
Diego, I made a mistake.

492
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:14,807
Yes, you did.

493
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:18,478
If it weren't for your womanizing,

494
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:22,190
none of this would've happened
to Lily or our family!

495
00:32:23,816 --> 00:32:26,152
What family? Huh?

496
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:31,115
You and I are the only family here, Diego.

497
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:34,369
Just the two of us. Do you understand?

498
00:32:36,871 --> 00:32:39,916
-What are you talking about?
-Listen.

499
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:44,462
Dad, stop it! Don't drag me
into this family's mess!

500
00:32:46,839 --> 00:32:47,840
Diego…

501
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:54,681
You aren't related to the Ardientes.

502
00:32:55,598 --> 00:32:59,185
Not to Emilia, or Julio…

503
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:03,773
Emilia's not your real mother.

504
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:05,191
[suspenseful sting]

505
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:11,531
Diego.

506
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:14,325
I'm sorry.

507
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,456
[young Diego crying] <i>Ouch!</i>

508
00:33:21,207 --> 00:33:22,208
[Julio] <i>Feel the pain!</i>

509
00:33:22,291 --> 00:33:25,003
<i>You have to become a real Ardiente!</i>

510
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:28,381
<i>I really don't understand</i>
<i>how you can be an Ardiente.</i>

511
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:31,759
<i>You're the only disgrace to this family.</i>

512
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,886
[young Arnaldo] <i>You don't act</i>
<i>like an Ardiente.</i>

513
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:36,889
<i>There's no weak Ardiente.</i>

514
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:40,810
So that's why.

515
00:33:43,771 --> 00:33:45,606
That's why they treat me like this.

516
00:33:46,482 --> 00:33:47,608
And you, Dad…

517
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:52,488
You hid it from me?

518
00:33:54,323 --> 00:33:55,241
Why?

519
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,326
Son, I'm on your side.

520
00:33:57,410 --> 00:34:00,872
Son, I'm here… Son… Son, listen--

521
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:03,332
All my life, I believed in you.

522
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:06,502
-I know I'm not perfect…
-What kind of father are you?

523
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:09,756
I've never been a perfect dad,
but I'll never leave you.

524
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:13,843
-I'll fix this.
-Dad, stop it. Stop.

525
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:16,262
[panting]

526
00:34:16,804 --> 00:34:19,891
You're a worthless father.
You're just like them.

527
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:22,727
-You are just like them!
-It's just you and me…

528
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:25,063
Diego… Diego! Diego!

529
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:27,857
Son! Son!

530
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:31,944
Diego!

531
00:34:35,948 --> 00:34:37,867
[panting]

532
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,088
[sobbing]

533
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:57,303
[melancholic music playing]

534
00:35:08,022 --> 00:35:11,609
-Ma'am, the guards are gone.
-Okay, good.

535
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:17,698
[dramatic music]

536
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:18,783
Madrigal.

537
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:21,953
Stay where you are.

538
00:35:26,207 --> 00:35:27,208
Emilia.

539
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,254
You told me to trust you.

540
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:35,716
You promised you would change.

541
00:35:37,343 --> 00:35:42,807
Killing is the only thing you know,
and yet, you still fail.

542
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:44,767
[Julio scoffs]

543
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:48,604
How is Camia Cruz still alive?

544
00:35:49,188 --> 00:35:52,733
-I will fix this problem, Papa.
-What? You?

545
00:35:53,609 --> 00:35:56,696
I'm sure you'll fail again.
I don't want you

546
00:35:56,779 --> 00:36:00,449
to have anything to do
with catching that woman.

547
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:02,660
But I will.

548
00:36:05,413 --> 00:36:08,082
I will fix this problem.

549
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,170
[Julio] Go!

550
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:19,468
Wait, what are you doing?
Wait, Papa! Papa! Please!

551
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:22,847
-[door closes]
-Papa! Papa!

552
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:27,101
Don't lock me up in here!
[pounding on door]

553
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:30,938
Papa! Open the door!

554
00:36:34,150 --> 00:36:35,484
[Emilia pounds on door]

555
00:36:37,570 --> 00:36:38,571
Papa!

556
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:43,993
[dramatic music playing]

557
00:36:53,461 --> 00:36:54,462
[exhales]

558
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:58,841
Hmph!

559
00:37:03,137 --> 00:37:04,180
Arnaldo?

560
00:37:05,514 --> 00:37:07,016
-Arnaldo.
-[door closes]

561
00:37:07,099 --> 00:37:08,517
You have to get me out of here.

562
00:37:08,601 --> 00:37:11,812
Please help me, son. I need to find Camia.

563
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:15,775
I mean, this is all my fault,
so let me pay for this.

564
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:18,736
No. You will do nothing, okay?

565
00:37:18,819 --> 00:37:21,697
Grandpa already ordered us
to look for Camia.

566
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:26,327
But, Arnaldo, I feel so useless.
Son, look at me.

567
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:29,747
I'm the former governor of Ardiente.

568
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:31,958
And now, I'm locked here.

569
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:34,502
I'm locked here! I'm locked here!

570
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:37,380
You can't look for her, okay?

571
00:37:37,463 --> 00:37:39,006
First of all, you have no machinery.

572
00:37:39,090 --> 00:37:41,884
And I can't provide you with that
because Grandpa will find out.

573
00:37:42,468 --> 00:37:47,390
Then let me make my
own machinery, my own empire.

574
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:54,146
-How will you do that?
-Take me to Ivy Aguas.

575
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:57,817
[tense music playing]

576
00:38:00,319 --> 00:38:03,114
[Ivy] Jepoy, thank you
for bringing these over.

577
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:05,825
I'm sure this will help Mom.

578
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:08,703
How's she doing?

579
00:38:10,913 --> 00:38:12,331
She's still sick.

580
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:31,517
Jepoy, what's wrong?

581
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:33,811
Are you okay?

582
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:36,397
[sighs]

583
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:39,358
Ivy. We need to keep
a closer eye on your mom.

584
00:38:39,442 --> 00:38:41,944
Emilia knows she was
in that burned-down house.

585
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:44,030
And she suspects she's still alive.

586
00:38:49,285 --> 00:38:50,286
Does she?

587
00:38:51,454 --> 00:38:55,458
Then I need to be ready in case
Emilia figures us out.

588
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:57,752
[tense music playing]

589
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:06,802
[sighs]

590
00:39:09,972 --> 00:39:12,850
-Okay, thank you.
-Well?

591
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,685
There's a certain rest house in Bataan

592
00:39:14,769 --> 00:39:17,980
that doesn't accept guests,
and it's owned by Aguas Realty.

593
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:20,024
Then…

594
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:24,362
You know, son, we should go now.
Let's go there.

595
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:27,365
Mom, this is the only time
I'm going to do this.

596
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:33,829
I know, son. I'm really thankful to you.

597
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:39,710
Just you?

598
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,088
I was expecting more of you here.

599
00:39:42,171 --> 00:39:44,507
-Where are the others?
-They're on their way, ma'am.

600
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:48,010
Okay. This is what you'll do.

601
00:39:48,094 --> 00:39:52,640
I want all of you to guard every
nook and cranny of this resort.

602
00:39:52,723 --> 00:39:55,267
-Do you understand?
-Yes, ma'am. As you wish.

603
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:56,811
That'll be all.

604
00:39:58,062 --> 00:39:59,230
[bodyguard] Check upstairs.

605
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:10,825
[slow instrumental playing]

606
00:40:28,801 --> 00:40:31,095
[Camia crying, banging on door]

607
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:48,654
[door opens]

608
00:40:55,327 --> 00:40:56,328
Mom?

609
00:40:58,789 --> 00:41:01,375
What's wrong, Mom? Mom.

610
00:41:02,668 --> 00:41:04,211
What's happening to you?

611
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:05,796
[panting]

612
00:41:06,088 --> 00:41:07,715
Don't you like it here?

613
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:11,135
I'll move you to another room,
or we can leave if you want.

614
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:13,596
[Raul] <i>It'd be for the best</i>
<i>if we go away for now.</i>

615
00:41:13,679 --> 00:41:15,014
<i>We're moving away from here.</i>

616
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:16,390
[Camia screaming]

617
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,478
-Leave?
-Yes.

618
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:24,398
No. I want to stay. I don't want to leave.

619
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:27,109
-Are you sure?
-I don't want to.

620
00:41:27,193 --> 00:41:30,863
Don't make me leave. I wanna stay.

621
00:41:30,946 --> 00:41:32,114
-I wanna stay.
-Okay, Mom.

622
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:34,325
I'm staying here. I'm not leaving!

623
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:38,120
-I don't want to leave!
-Okay, Mom. We won't.

624
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:39,622
We won't leave.

625
00:41:39,705 --> 00:41:40,956
-I don't want to leave.
-We're not leaving.

626
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:44,001
You can stay here, Mom. Calm down.

627
00:41:46,128 --> 00:41:48,130
[tense music playing]

628
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:55,513
Mom, sit down.

629
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:00,851
Ivy.

630
00:42:02,394 --> 00:42:03,521
I'm so sorry.

631
00:42:03,604 --> 00:42:07,233
It's all right, Mom.
You don't have to apologize.

632
00:42:08,067 --> 00:42:10,027
I'll leave you for a moment.

633
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:12,696
Uh…

634
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:14,281
What are those?

635
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:20,579
Books and other stuff.

636
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:26,627
They might help jog your memories, Mom.

637
00:42:26,710 --> 00:42:29,964
But you can take a look
at these once you've rested.

638
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:31,173
Oh, no.

639
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,009
I want to see them.

640
00:42:36,804 --> 00:42:37,680
All right.

641
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:44,520
[slow instrumental playing]

642
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,610
Mom, these books…

643
00:42:53,487 --> 00:42:57,533
they're what you used
when you were still teaching.

644
00:43:06,333 --> 00:43:07,334
And this.

645
00:43:09,003 --> 00:43:10,379
This notebook…

646
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:14,633
Dad wrote…

647
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:19,221
<i>365 Days of Love and Guidance</i>…

648
00:43:20,681 --> 00:43:23,601
as a guide for me when I grow up.

649
00:43:29,940 --> 00:43:32,943
[somber music playing]

650
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:40,826
This is you, Mom.

651
00:43:43,829 --> 00:43:45,331
This is Dad.

652
00:43:48,959 --> 00:43:51,754
And this is… Lily.

653
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:02,348
Dante?

654
00:44:06,769 --> 00:44:07,770
Lily.

655
00:44:12,816 --> 00:44:13,817
Lily.

656
00:44:15,694 --> 00:44:18,989
Lily, my daughter. My daughter, Lily.

657
00:44:26,830 --> 00:44:27,831
Lily.

658
00:44:31,251 --> 00:44:32,086
Lily.

659
00:44:37,216 --> 00:44:38,258
[Emilia] <i>Hi. Good morning.</i>

660
00:44:38,342 --> 00:44:40,386
<i>-Is Miss Aguas here?</i>
<i>-I'm sorry.</i>

661
00:44:40,469 --> 00:44:42,763
<i>We aren't accepting</i>
<i>any visitors at the moment.</i>

662
00:44:42,846 --> 00:44:45,724
-<i>We aren't your typical guests.</i>
-[Diego] <i>They killed my mother!</i>

663
00:44:45,808 --> 00:44:46,767
<i>Where's the justice?</i>

664
00:44:46,850 --> 00:44:48,727
-<i>The Ardientes will kill you…</i>
-[Loring] <i>Pandoy!</i>

665
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:50,479
<i>…if you go against them!</i>

666
00:44:50,562 --> 00:44:52,022
[Emilia] <i>I need a huge sum of money</i>

667
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:58,070
<i>to get back into power and stop</i>
<i>my enemies' plans against me.</i>

668
00:44:58,153 --> 00:44:59,696
<i>Like this one person.</i>

669
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:02,366
<i>I don't know if you're</i>
<i>familiar with her. Camia Cruz?</i>

670
00:45:03,158 --> 00:45:05,869
-[Camia] <i>Ouch! Stop it!</i>
-[glass shattering]

671
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:07,371
[Emilia] <i>What's that sound?</i>

672
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:08,831
[Arnaldo] <i>Why are there nurses here?</i>

673
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:13,210
[theme music playing]
